Ok, it's 11:00 PM and I finished the game that I now have more than 36 hours
invested in. Guido the Spelunker ascended to Demi-God with 1324758 points.

THANKS to all you wizards who wrote a lot of stuff between the lines in
your postings that I was able to figure out and apply to my game.

Potential Spoilers Follow

A few observations/Questions:
1) I genocided all liches from the moment I encountered the first one (using
   blessed scroll), but later I saw a demilich named Sam. Obviously a Quantum
   mechanic stepped on a polymorph trap and morphed into one. Is this a bug?

2) Right up front, I'll admit that I kept save files around. Not so much to
   keep going back to when I died, although I did do that a few times, but
   more because the Macintosh version is a little unstable. Anyone else
   notice this? 
   
   *** Mac Hacks Only ***
   Occasionally (i.e. not repeatable), I get thrown into Macsbug with a Bus 
   Error when 0xFFFFFFF8 gets read. This happens when the Yes/No box is 
   thrown up, usually in reference to a tasty morsel on the ground and do I 
   want to eat it.  I have a IIci, 20" Radius Monitor with Radius SuperColor
   board, 20MB RAM with NetHack using 1.536 MB. I'm not running any wierd 
   extensions: System 7, file sharing, SuperClock, MacTCP, MS Mail, PKey,
   After Dark, NowMenus, QuickColor (Radius Color Extension), RadiusWare.
   No Virtual Memory.

3) I've always played Barbarians and Cavemen because they started out strong,
   but as I've gotten better, I started playing wizards. While it is nice to
   occasionally get wands and spellbooks at startup, I find that I don't use
   wands much, but I use the heck out of holy water. That's when I started to
   play priests. As I got to where I could find the cursed/blessed status
   using other means, I decided to challenge myself and play archeologist.

   My whole motive for that decision was greed--I wanted the best gems
   possible. I'm surprised that a dilithium crystal is worth only 500 
   zorkmids more than a diamond. Are cursed gems worth less than uncursed
   ones?

4) Toward the end, eating a giant corpse only gave me /01 increase in
   strength. For a while, I had Gauntlets of Strength, but I couldn't lift
   anything more with them as without. Any ideas? They were +0.

5) Once, I polymorphed ten throwing stars into 10 two handed swords. I picked
   up two and wielded them, and it said "2 Two Handed Swords (wielded)". What
   did this really mean?  Did I have a two handed sword in each hand? When I
   dropped one, I got "a Two Handed Sword (weapon in hand)".  
   
6) I didn't polypile too much, I cancelled all my unneeded scrolls, blessed
   them, then morphed them into identify scrolls and enchant armor and
   enchant weapon.

7) At first, I liked the notion of not teleporting once you had intrinsic
   teleport and intrinsic teleport control with ^T ability. In fact, after
   I read that post, I was walking around on level 35, triggered a land
   mine while on my way to pick up my food rations that I'd dropped, so
   I'd stop being hungry. Since I had too much stuff, I was collapsing, and
   since I was hungry and fast becoming weak, I didn't have the strength to
   ^T! Fortunately as I dropped my $45000, I got a random teleport and was
   able to eat.

8) I hate it when I polymorph into a dragon, then polymorph again and lose
   my dragon scale mail! It's a good thing I had a pretty good intrinsic AC
   until I could create a new set of dragon mail.

9) What does a spellbook of wizard lock do?

10) What protects me from the Touch of Death that the Wiz has? If it weren't
    for my amulet of life saving, I'd have been toast as I walked into
    Quetzalcotl's altar in the endgame.

11) I didn't get a single wish. The only magic lamp I encountered, when rubbed,
    seriously annoyed the djinni. "You disturbed me, fool!" Then he started
    to beat on me. Fortunately, he was an easy kill. Should I have done this?
    The WoW in the castle had 0 charges and the charging scroll blew it up!

12) The Wiz was on level 32. I spent a lot of time dicking around on the
    lower levels because I forgot to grab a mirror on my way down. It was
    good luck that I encountered a beastie with one on level 43. The Wiz
    didn't attack me but twice during my ascent--Levels 30 and 1.

13) I found a beehive that had to be as large as a room could get. When all
    was said and done, I got 17 lumps of royal jelly! Yum Yum!

I did this with 
 Blessed +0 Green Dragon Scale Mail, 
 Blessed +3 Speed Boots,
 Blessed +3 Gauntlets of Dexterity, 
 Blessed +0 Shield of Reflection. 
 
My Strength was 18/90. I had Blessed +4 Mjollnir (given by Quetzalcotl). I like
Mjollnir! Much more effective than Excalibur or Frost Brand. With it, I didn't
bother trying to get DragonBane or DemonBane, either.

I think I'd better stop playing for a while. I'm lucky that my wife was out
of town this weekend, or I would have seriously annoyed her and then she
would have started beating on me. I don't think she would have been as easy
a kill as the djinni! :-)

